<article class="env-corollary" id="82F8D7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/82F8D7">Corollary <span data-tag="82F8D7">4.1.2.2</span>.</a> Suppose given maps $A \stackrel{i}{\rightarrow } B \stackrel{j}{\rightarrow } C$ of simplicial sets. If $i$ and $j \circ i$ are right anodyne, and $j$ is a cofibration, then $j$ is right-anodyne. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Proposition <a href="/tag/4F4564" data-tag="4F4564">4.1.2.1</a>, $i$ and $j \circ i$ are contravariant equivalences in $(\sSet )_{/C}$. It follows that $j$ is a trivial cofibration in $(\sSet )_{/C}$, so that $j$ is right anodyne (by Proposition <a href="/tag/4F4564" data-tag="4F4564">4.1.2.1</a> again). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>